WEBVTT

NOTE Generated from the locked Scaffold narration and edit timeline.

1
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.730
A digital lesson can be much more than text followed by a quiz.

2
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:22.242
Scaffold lets authors work directly with the lesson they are creating.

3
00:00:22.242 --> 00:00:26.123
Text, media and layout remain visible while every change happens in context.

4
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:35.686
Select a block to reveal its quick controls.

5
00:00:35.686 --> 00:00:40.837
Change its layout and make common adjustments without opening a separate editing screen.

6
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.520
For deeper changes, open the settings sheet.

7
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:52.210
Change the chart type, edit its data, map columns,

8
00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.490
and control its appearance without leaving the lesson.

9
00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:05.477
Writing tools appear exactly where they are needed.

10
00:01:05.477 --> 00:01:10.167
Select text to format it, define vocabulary,

11
00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:15.527
or add mathematical notation directly where it appears.

12
00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:24.237
Use the toolbar on the left to create headings, lists, quotations and code.

13
00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:35.842
Browse the block library on the right,

14
00:01:35.842 --> 00:01:40.223
or type a slash where you are working to search the same collection.

15
00:01:40.223 --> 00:01:44.603
Choose a block and Scaffold adds it at that position, ready to configure.

16
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:52.453
Assessment is built into the lesson.

17
00:01:52.453 --> 00:01:57.514
Authors can set the correct response, write feedback for each choice, add hints,

18
00:01:57.514 --> 00:02:01.797
limit attempts, and decide how many points the question is worth.

19
00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:11.536
Learners submit when they are ready and receive feedback written for the answer they chose.

20
00:02:11.536 --> 00:02:15.149
When another attempt is allowed, Try again resets the question

21
00:02:15.149 --> 00:02:17.317
so they can reconsider their response.

22
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:23.626
Multiple choice is only one option.

23
00:02:23.626 --> 00:02:27.604
Scaffold also includes matching, sequencing, categorisation, fill-in-the-blanks,

24
00:02:27.604 --> 00:02:34.424
multi-select, dropdown, image hotspots and complete quizzes, all with the same feedback,

25
00:02:34.424 --> 00:02:36.697
attempts and scoring controls.

26
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.223
Scaffold can also become a guided presentation.

27
00:02:44.223 --> 00:02:47.659
The same visual building blocks move through full-image scenes

28
00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:49.950
and layouts designed slide by slide.

29
00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.758
Different slide layouts let you shape the presentation around the content.

30
00:02:53.758 --> 00:02:56.674
In two columns, you can adjust the balance between regions

31
00:02:56.674 --> 00:02:59.590
and hide the title when you need the full canvas.

32
00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.866
Each column can hold more than one block.

33
00:03:04.866 --> 00:03:07.696
Tabs bring a reading, images, an audio field note

34
00:03:07.696 --> 00:03:11.470
and an explanatory video together in the same part of the slide.

35
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.299
You can place a comprehension question beside the material it relates to,

36
00:03:16.299 --> 00:03:20.010
so learners can examine the evidence without switching between separate screens.

37
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:24.239
In preview, learners can move between the reading, audio and video

38
00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:25.824
and scroll through each one.

39
00:03:25.824 --> 00:03:29.630
The question remains visible beside them while they work out the answer.

40
00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.793
Scaffold brings the whole lesson together in one visual workflow.

41
00:03:35.793 --> 00:03:39.910
Authors can combine explanation, media and assessment, while learners explore, practise

42
00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:42.530
and receive feedback in the same place.
